  "notes": "DELIBERATE STRESS CASE for Phase 2's stitcher/column-drift detector (task 2.3). PyMuPDF's raw find_tables() reports a different physical column count per page (12, 14, 13, 30) because merged header cells produce extra blank/sliver grid columns that shift depending on which cell spans which page's row. The 10 `column_headers` above are the *semantic* columns (same across all 4 pages); page 21's PK/ADA/Tumor Biopsy rows are cross-references to separate flow charts whose text spans every column, recorded as a mark in data column 0 under the non-empty-cell convention; `marks` indices are hand-aligned to that semantic scheme, not to PyMuPDF's raw per-page column index -- this is exactly the kind of column-count mismatch a naive stitcher must detect and either resolve or hard-fail on (DESIGN.md L2), never silently misalign. Two section-divider rows ('Laboratory Assessments', 'Disease Assessment') are excluded from `activities`."
